  "instructions": [
    "heat 1/2 cup coconut oil in a large paella pan over medium-high heat.",
    "add onion and bell pepper and sauté for 5 minutes.",
    "add garlic and sauté for 1 minute.",
    "add clams, namul blanch season, Jamaican curry powder, allspice, oregano, and chicken broth.",
    "stir well, bring to a boil, then reduce heat to low.",
    "cover with a lid and simmer for 10 minutes, or until clams open.",
    "add coconut milk and lemon juice, stir well.",
    "continue to simmer for 2 minutes, or until sauce thickens.",
    "serve hot, garnish with oregano and lemon wedges."
